      "source": [
        "# OAI KL-grade — beat the 82% SOTA (ROI @224 + CleanLab-aggressive labels)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal:** exceed the published **82.12%** on OAI 5-class, on the **same protocol the SOTA uses** — accuracy against CleanLab-*corrected* labels.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why this can work (from your own results):** ROI cropping gave **+2.8 pp**; raising resolution *failed* on corrected labels (384px aggressive = 76.9%, because a hi-res model diverges from the 224-defined corrected labels). So the untried winning move is **ROI @224**, not more pixels.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Fair-claim rules (baked in):**\n",
        "- The CleanLab cleaning step is **identical** to your 81% run: ConvNeXt-Small out-of-fold on the 224px images. Only the **classifier** is upgraded (ROI crop). → the gain is real, not extra circularity.\n",
        "- Reported metric = **corrected-label accuracy** (same as the SOTA paper). Original-label accuracy is printed alongside for honesty.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Order:** setup → core → (opt) 384px regen → load + CleanLab OOF (cached) → aggressive relabel → fixed split → ROI crops → transfer corrected labels onto ROI → train ConvNeXt-Base @224 (+opt ensemble) + TTA → result vs 82.12%.\n",
        "\n",
        "Run top to bottom. Heavy steps (CleanLab OOF, training) cache/checkpoint, so re-runs are cheap."
      ],
      "id": "Cx3gZDXi10EG"
    },
